<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Operating System Guide</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #f5f1ff;
            padding: 30px;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 850px;
            margin: auto;
            background: white;
            padding: 30px;
            border-radius: 18px;
        }

        h1 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #633bb5;
        }

        .os {
            padding: 18px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            background: #f0eaff;
            border-radius: 12px;
        }

        h2 {
            color: #633bb5;
        }

        li {
            margin: 8px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="container">

    <h1>⚙️ Operating System Guide</h1>

    <div class="os">
        <h2>What is an Operating System?</h2>
        <p>
            An operating system is system software that manages computer
            hardware and provides services for applications.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="os">
        <h2>Examples</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Windows</li>
            <li>Linux</li>
            <li>macOS</li>
            <li>Android</li>
            <li>iOS</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="os">
        <h2>Main Functions</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Memory management</li>
            <li>File management</li>
            <li>Process management</li>
            <li>Device management</li>
            <li>Security management</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

</div>

</body>
</html>
